<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $36.7 mln Jan 21.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $36.7 mln Jan 21.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $36.7 million surplus on Jan 21 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JANUARY 21</p>
<p>Exports: $354.4 million</p>
<p>Imports: $332.1 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $380.1 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $365.7 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $36.7 million</p>
<p>JANUARY DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.049 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $3.003 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $4.304 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.441 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $909 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2485418))</p>
</text>
